                "retweet_count": 737,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "In 1935, the U.S. Supreme Court held that a tax that doesn\u2019t generate revenue cannot be justified as a tax.\n\nIn 1937, the U.S. Supreme Court also held that the NFA\u2019s registration was a constitutional exercise of Congress\u2019s taxation power.\n\nSo, when Congress zeroed out NFA taxes for SBRs, SBSs, AOWs, and suppressors in the One Big Beautiful Bill, we eliminated the so-called constitutional foundation for NFA registration.\n\nArguing otherwise is incongruent with congressional intent, U.S. Supreme Court precedent, and the Second Amendment.",
